{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge","id":1305603,"title":"A Possible Change To The Lucifuge.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-17T17:53:31-07:00","id":1305603,"title":"A Possible Change To The Lucifuge.","content":"Hey! So, i wa reading the Contagion thread and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> pointed out something interesting. One of the powers presented in the contagion chronicle allows hunters and others beings to becomg godlike for a while. And the Lucifuge are used as a example,it was said they become the god they told other people they can become as well. Which begs the question,are Lucifuge changing for penintent redemption and salvation seekers to a more modern satanist tranhumanist faction? One that is about gaining power ? what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:38:16-07:00","id":1305860,"title":"","content":"It'd be a fairly odd path to take, given the core book hunter's general focus on &quot;humanity&quot; rather than the arguable transhumanist states of the other book's monsters. From the 2E playtest, we can see they're still fighting against their demon side rather than embracing it (...at least for the most part). Nothing really about gaining power, bunch about fighting your inner demons and how they're gonna be made if you let yourself loose.<br /> <br /> I'm not caught up with my Contagion, and it did feel like they where stepping away from the heavier Christian demon imagery with the God-Machine angel/demon stuff in Mortal Remains, but I doubt they're going the &quot;Being a half demon is totally awesome&quot; route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:32:44-07:00","id":1305871,"title":"","content":"honestly I hope they stay with the original themes more, a change so drastic seems unnecessary (and the demon section for them could of been better IMO)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T09:39:42-07:00","id":1306023,"title":"","content":"So with the new Contagion preview, we also discover that they may shift the Lucifuge's origin from Inferno to the God Machine (something which was straight ruled out in Mortal Remains). I'm not sure how I feel about it, if it is true. Will have to wait for more info before I'll judge.<br /> <br /> Also, it looks like the AKD are officially the ones getting the cut as a core conspiracy, as they are the only ones not mentioned in the writeup among the big six, and their place is taken by the Council of Bones (the Ashwood Abbey is replaced by some group called S.W.O.R.N, which seem to have connections with native american tribes, but we already knew that the Abbey was cut as a core and sent to a short writeup, so no surprise here)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T10:20:02-07:00","id":1306033,"title":"","content":"not gonna lie, I dont like the replacement of the abbey and AKD (though the council sounds cool at least, in terms of name)<br /> <br /> though, what really disappoints me is the possible lucifuge shift. hopefully the AKD and abbey get into a supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:12:54-07:00","id":1306130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306023#post1306023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the new Contagion preview, we also discover that they may shift the Lucifuge's origin from Inferno to the God Machine (something which was straight ruled out in Mortal Remains).</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no, Lost. Inferno never actually offered a conclusive origin for the Lucifuge (it would be supremely bad signposting to put a definite answer to a gameline-specific splat's origins in a bluebook), Mortal Remains doesn't &quot;straight rule out&quot; any of the Lucifuge having origins in the Unchained or their maker (the opposite is outright floated as one of their fears), and the Bend preview doesn't do any more than posit the <i>possibility</i> that <i>some</i> of its hunters <i>might</i> draw a line of descent from the God-Machine (which is no more a change to their origin than Mortal Remains's putting up speculation that the conspiracy's patron has some connection to the True Fae).<br /> <br /> Hunter's relation to the wider cosmology is weird and the Lucifuge's only definitive unifying feature has historically been &quot;they work for the Lucifuge.&quot; That doesn't change if some of them are the product of long-term Infrastructural oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:39:09-07:00","id":1306148,"title":"","content":"The Lucifuge always have and always will started the initial approach of self-understanding from a Milton-esque mythopoeic point of view in a world that is decidely non-mythopoeic, but as a group of children of demons run into the problem of a world where &quot;Did you mean demon, demon, or demon?&quot; is a thing, it becomes increasingly clear where foreign influences got roped into a barely-fitting mask. This is why Castigations cast the broader net that they do, and is <i>entirely</i> the reason why The Truth have enough ammo to be a discernible faction-because as the edges of understanding become cracked by just how much of a mixed family tree the Lucifuge really is, the more and more you have to wonder just who the damnedable woman leading this little lie told <i>really </i>is.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm starting to want to burn out the section in the Inferno with how often that section comes up and is used a means to ignore <i>the rest of the text across the entire line</i>.<br /> <br /> ANyways, as far as Bend is concerned, It's not surprising that plays a little more emphasis on those with more discernable techgnostic ties, considering the way that the G-M relates to the contagion within text. Still, no more so than the Changeling Chapter of Mortal Remains asserting the critical analysis of Lucifige as children of fairies should be taken as an absolute, the reading of Bend should not be used to reflect widely on the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> The devil is in the details, and the world is <i>lousy</i> with devils. It's crass to assume you've got the full picture when you're at the bottom of the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-20-2019, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T09:32:32-07:00","id":1306267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306023#post1306023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the new Contagion preview, we also discover that they may shift the Lucifuge's origin from Inferno to the God Machine (something which was straight ruled out in Mortal Remains). I'm not sure how I feel about it, if it is true. Will have to wait for more info before I'll judge.<br /> <br /> Also, it looks like the AKD are officially the ones getting the cut as a core conspiracy, as they are the only ones not mentioned in the writeup among the big six, and their place is taken by the Council of Bones (the Ashwood Abbey is replaced by some group called S.W.O.R.N, which seem to have connections with native american tribes, but we already knew that the Abbey was cut as a core and sent to a short writeup, so no surprise here)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of supuprised. I thought that the &quot;a conspiracy is getting cut&quot; thing was a misunderstanding? A miscount or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:43:46-07:00","id":1306331,"title":"","content":"Wait conspiracies are getting cut? Is there a dev blog or forum post that confirms with reasoning? Not trying to complain just curious as to why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:12:42-07:00","id":1306363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madman777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306331#post1306331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait conspiracies are getting cut? Is there a dev blog or forum post that confirms with reasoning? Not trying to complain just curious as to why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Ashwood Abbey was cut due to dislike for the Compact (it being a club of rich people out to have a good time by killing monsters), but that could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Dunno why they would cut the AKD, other than that I liked it. ;(<br /> <br /> But I think that both are being relegated to a sidebar as being mentioned like most of the minor compacts and conspiracies, and that they might receive a full write up in a supplement book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T08:21:14-07:00","id":1306530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306363#post1306363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Ashwood Abbey was cut due to dislike for the Compact (it being a club of rich people out to have a good time by killing monsters), but that could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Dunno why they would cut the AKD, other than that I liked it. ;(<br /> <br /> But I think that both are being relegated to a sidebar as being mentioned like most of the minor compacts and conspiracies, and that they might receive a full write up in a supplement book.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's what I'm hoping for. the ashwood were getting so much better as the supplements went on into more than just &quot;killing for fun&quot; into being the compact that interacted with monsters in all ways for a thrill. no idea why AKD was cut, hopefully both make a supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T22:43:07-07:00","id":1307690,"title":"","content":"Is the bend preview public? I want to have a quick read about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23615-pierrew","user":"Pierrew","date":". 04-25-2019, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23615-pierrew","name":"Pierrew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:33:01-07:00","id":1307779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pierrew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307690#post1307690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the bend preview public? I want to have a quick read about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>you have to back the kickstarter to see it. do it quickly it will be over is less than 2 hours","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T14:56:02-07:00","id":1307855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306363#post1306363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Ashwood Abbey was cut due to dislike for the Compact (it being a club of rich people out to have a good time by killing monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't usually that base premise so much as how the corebook pretty heavily presented them as &quot;If you're lucky they'll kill you [I]before[/] they rape and skin you&quot; which is... very niche where being meant as protagonists is concerned. Compacts &amp; Conspiracies made a valiant effort (which their eventual 2e depiction will presumably continue) to turn back on that being the default member but the damage was already done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T15:03:37-07:00","id":1307858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307855#post1307855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem isn't usually that base premise so much as how the corebook pretty heavily presented them as &quot;If you're lucky they'll kill you [I]before[/] they rape and skin you&quot; which is... very niche where being meant as protagonists is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core didn't really do this, but the durability of the 'Ashwood Abbey are all rapists' meme did likely contribute to their being cut and overall dislike for the compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T19:46:14-07:00","id":1307925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307858#post1307858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The core didn't really do this, but the durability of the 'Ashwood Abbey are all rapists' meme did likely contribute to their being cut and overall dislike for the compact.</div> </div> </div> </div>very true. while the corebook did lack the variety of ways the abbey interacts with the supernatural (as a natural hellfire club would), the opening fiction for them and paragraphs were memed to hell until people were just unwilling to give them a chance. as others have said and as I've said, here is hoping that they (and the AKD) make it to a supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:59:56-07:00","id":1307947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1306363#post1306363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Ashwood Abbey was cut due to dislike for the Compact (it being a club of rich people out to have a good time by killing monsters), but that could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Dunno why they would cut the AKD, other than that I liked it. ;(<br /> <br /> But I think that both are being relegated to a sidebar as being mentioned like most of the minor compacts and conspiracies, and that they might receive a full write up in a supplement book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they cut the AKD to make way for the Circle of Bones.<br /> <br /> Who are apparently necromancers and shamans for justice.<br /> <br /> Can't really complain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:45:12-07:00","id":1307969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307947#post1307947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think they cut the AKD to make way for the Circle of Bones.<br /> <br /> Who are apparently necromancers and shamans for justice.<br /> <br /> Can't really complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but I was a really big fan of the AKD. I liked their usage of magic through artifacts and how you could essentially be Indiana Jones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T23:55:47-07:00","id":1307982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307969#post1307969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair, but I was a really big fan of the AKD. I liked their usage of magic through artifacts and how you could essentially be Indiana Jones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling we might see their organisation in Mummy 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T00:33:09-07:00","id":1307987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1307982#post1307982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling we might see their organisation in Mummy 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm probably not gonna buy Mummy 2e since I don't see my group actually playing that line, so I'mma hold out hope for them ending up in a Hunter supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T16:42:24-07:00","id":1309324,"title":"","content":"As someone with transhumanist leanings, I do <i>not</i> like the idea of a transhumanist Lucifuge. Before, they were about struggling to overcome what they were born into, and standing up for humankind; this seems to shift them towards &quot;I am better because I was born better&quot; powerfantasy. The ideal of transhumanism is lifting up oneself and others to overcome the frailties of what evolution gave us; being granted innately superior powers from birth, by circumstances outside your control, is the inverse of that. It is the aristocracy to transhumanism's meritocracy. What's more, the Lucifuges' humility, bordering on self-hatred, is what kept them from becoming superhero cliches. Hunter is about the worth of human life, and defending that candle against those that would snuff it out. Making a group about &quot;being born better than humans, and getting more better&quot; spits on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 05-02-2019, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T09:23:42-07:00","id":1309463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1309324#post1309324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with transhumanist leanings, I do <i>not</i> like the idea of a transhumanist Lucifuge. Before, they were about struggling to overcome what they were born into, and standing up for humankind; this seems to shift them towards &quot;I am better because I was born better&quot; powerfantasy. The ideal of transhumanism is lifting up oneself and others to overcome the frailties of what evolution gave us; being granted innately superior powers from birth, by circumstances outside your control, is the inverse of that. It is the aristocracy to transhumanism's meritocracy. What's more, the Lucifuges' humility, bordering on self-hatred, is what kept them from becoming superhero cliches. Hunter is about the worth of human life, and defending that candle against those that would snuff it out. Making a group about &quot;being born better than humans, and getting more better&quot; spit on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you. the Lucifuge will be &quot;just another satanic spawn&quot; trope if they love what they are. the self hatred they have in their mindset and using it for more heroic ends make them much more interesting (and we could explore the cruel practices the Lucifuge does when recruiting. this new take would just be &quot;you are cursed with awesome power, enjoy it but be responsible&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 05-02-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T18:34:55-07:00","id":1310643,"title":"","content":"Disappointed to hear AKD may be cut. Hope they're still in the line later even if not in the core. The combination of Indiana Jones + Warehouse 13 is such an obvious hook. I was hoping 2e would take the focus off werewolves to put it where it belongs on the Mage/Mummy overlap for their foes - which fits with for how I'm using them in Vigil for Rome, as the Constantinople HQed Nicaean Christian Conspiracy breaking the power of Gnostic sorcerers and putting down dark false gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-07-2019, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:26:17-07:00","id":1310648,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> I hope any 2e incarnation of AKD will actually have a way of dealing with Awakened Mages. They're the only Hunter faction that differentiates between the Awakened and other spellcasters, yet they are Sleepers and have no relics or other abilities to offset that. The Malleus Maleficarum, who lump the Awakened in with all other &quot;witches,&quot; are far better equipped to actually deal with the Awakened by virtue of the fact they can at least remember that Supernal magic occurred, and even they are vastly outclassed and virtually incapable of dealing with the Awakened.<br /> <br /> But I agree re: Werewolves, I never understood what the Werewolves had to do with the AKD; Mummies, being competitors for relics, make far more sense as primary antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:39:14-07:00","id":1310649,"title":"","content":"On AKD and Werewolves: Aaaaaaargh. I don't have the spoons to explain it, but yes it actually make sense, I'll see if I can get to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:43:02-07:00","id":1310652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310648#post1310648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> I hope any 2e incarnation of AKD will actually have a way of dealing with Awakened Mages. They're the only Hunter faction that differentiates between the Awakened and other spellcasters, yet they are Sleepers and have no relics or other abilities to offset that. The Malleus Maleficarum, who lump the Awakened in with all other &quot;witches,&quot; are far better equipped to actually deal with the Awakened by virtue of the fact they can at least remember that Supernal magic occurred, and even they are vastly outclassed and virtually incapable of dealing with the Awakened.<br /> <br /> But I agree re: Werewolves, I never understood what the Werewolves had to do with the AKD; Mummies, being competitors for relics, make far more sense as primary antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly if you're doing a crossover with Hunter and MtA, you should just treat all Hunters as Sleepwalkers for free out of sheer fairness to the players. Just assume the Conspiracy in question seeks out people given to said awareness of the secret world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:57:43-07:00","id":1310659,"title":"","content":"I swear to god, this conversation has been done to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T20:04:25-07:00","id":1310660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310652#post1310652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly if you're doing a crossover with Hunter and MtA, you should just treat all Hunters as Sleepwalkers for free out of sheer fairness to the players. Just assume the Conspiracy in question seeks out people given to said awareness of the secret world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking crossover, exactly, just musing on the fact that the AKD are the only Hunter faction that cares about Awakened Mages as a separate group, but also doesn't have Sleepwalker status by default. If I had anyone in my Hunter game want to join the AKD I'd highly recommend they take Unseen Sense: the Supernal as a Merit; it's part of the 5-dot status benefit in Mortal Remains, but that comes really late.<br /> <br /> If they're going to change things up for 2e anyway, I just feel it's something that should be looked at.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T20:20:33-07:00","id":1310661,"title":"","content":"Not that it isn't worth revisting with a new rant, but in case y'all missed it, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227282#post227282\">here's the first time I ranted about people not getting that the central theme of the AKD is paradise lost.</a> <br /> <br /> The destruction of the world is a claim that only mages and werewolves claim. Even mummies, with the shattering of time, didn't fundamentally change the nature of the world the way either of those guys (mythologically or historically) did. It's that fundamental change to the world, the loss of Arcadia (to borrow from the Greeks), that the Guardians of the Labyrinth seek to redress and punish.<br /> <br /> The rest of who they are stems from this loss of paradise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T21:23:05-07:00","id":1310672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310659#post1310659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear to god, this conversation has been done to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might just break the forum with how active its been lately. Having a tired conversation is a step up from having none :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T21:29:17-07:00","id":1310673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310672#post1310672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We might just break the forum with how active its been lately. Having a tired conversation is a step up from having none :V</div> </div> </div> </div>Unpopular opinion, death before beating the dead horse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:48:27-07:00","id":1310718,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Arc on this one- to the AKD, relics are not the goal, but the means. The goal is vengeance mixed with jealousy, spiced with dreams about reclaiming what was once theirs, and is now denied of them. Werewolves and mages broke the world, and took from their ancestors their rightful place and inheritance. In short, to the AKD, mummies are rivals- but shifters and mages are the <i>enemies</i>, and that is a huge difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T05:39:16-07:00","id":1310728,"title":"","content":"The idea behind AKD might be solid, but the execution was muddied. They could fix it, but I'm fine with replacing them with something instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T06:52:35-07:00","id":1310738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310660#post1310660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking crossover, exactly, just musing on the fact that the AKD are the only Hunter faction that cares about Awakened Mages as a separate group, but also doesn't have Sleepwalker status by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true. There's the optional 'The Ancient Vow Made Manifest' section from C&amp;C. Keeping in mind that the rules on Sleepwalkers are deliberately vague, I'd say that could satisfy the requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T09:27:47-07:00","id":1310766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310718#post1310718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm with Arc on this one- to the AKD, relics are not the goal, but the means. The goal is vengeance mixed with jealousy, spiced with dreams about reclaiming what was once theirs, and is now denied of them. Werewolves and mages broke the world, and took from their ancestors their rightful place and inheritance. In short, to the AKD, mummies are rivals- but shifters and mages are the <i>enemies</i>, and that is a huge difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great phrasing!<br /> <br /> A lot of it comes down to presentation, and the AKD started on the wrong foot as that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T10:35:00-07:00","id":1310771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310718#post1310718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm with Arc on this one- to the AKD, relics are not the goal, but the means. The goal is vengeance mixed with jealousy, spiced with dreams about reclaiming what was once theirs, and is now denied of them. Werewolves and mages broke the world, and took from their ancestors their rightful place and inheritance. In short, to the AKD, mummies are rivals- but shifters and mages are the <i>enemies</i>, and that is a huge difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>It always felt backwards to me. More like &quot;OK, I have this cool idea for a group! They use magical relics despite being normal humans otherwise!&quot; &quot;I see, I see. So they're hunters, right? They'll probably end up fighting the type of monsters that have artifacts, so they can get more.&quot; &quot;Right, makes sense! So the big book monsters that have artifacts are...Mages and werewolves. Here, I'll write up a backstory giving them a reason to hunt them beyond killing them and taking their stuff!&quot;<br /> <br /> If the book where written now, it would certainly have &quot;and mummies&quot; tacked on if not shifting focus on them primarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T11:03:04-07:00","id":1310776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310771#post1310771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It always felt backwards to me. More like &quot;OK, I have this cool idea for a group! They use magical relics despite being normal humans otherwise!&quot; &quot;I see, I see. So they're hunters, right? They'll probably end up fighting the type of monsters that have artifacts, so they can get more.&quot; &quot;Right, makes sense! So the big book monsters that have artifacts are...Mages and werewolves. Here, I'll write up a backstory giving them a reason to hunt them beyond killing them and taking their stuff!&quot;<br /> <br /> If the book where written now, it would certainly have &quot;and mummies&quot; tacked on if not shifting focus on them primarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well<br /> <br /> a) It's not written now. It was written over a decade ago with several books of built up mythology, structure, modes of operation, and more, and with that, the focus has been clarified and developed, and to arbitrarily go &quot;Well NOW we know about this game, so, you know, shove it in there&quot; feels pretty damn disingenuous compared to the clear theme it has.<br /> <br /> b) You make it sound like that's not part of the design process. In this case, they started with the idiom of relics, which at the time covered werewolves, mages, and changelings. So they worked backwards to develop a story that was cool and evocative out of there, arrived at the destruction of a paradisical world, built into those themes(Because it is a major part of the text in Hunter 1E's Core, even if it's not the first part), cut out changelings because it didn't fit, and built their story from there. That's just how game design works. If you applied the same principle today, anyone looking for Cool, Evocative, and Weird is probably going to latch onto the same common root, and <i>maybe</i> create a hierarchy of enemies that allowed for emphasis on the Arisen, but would probably still give precedence to mages and werewolves. You don't always arrive where you start, but when you try to get to the heart of a thing and deal with strong ideas, you end up where you need to.<br /> <br /> c) Just because something sounds <i>obvious</i> doesn't mean it always work. You have to take a long hard look at the tangle of things and see how it spins out to find the really strong thread, and then ruthlessly shave things out in the holy name of word count, and keep your focus on that core. Paradise Lost is a stronger thread than Oh Hey Relics, and can in fact better support Relics than Relics could support, say, Paradise Lost. With that said, some things get lost as a result of that.<br /> <br /> d) In order to be horrifying, weird, tantalizing, and otherwise intriguing, what horror and comedy share is the twist of expectations. The sheer fact people complain about it without thinking about it but how it works with a little examination basically means the way AKD is now is a damn good fit for the dark mystery and horror angles of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;But They Both Care About Relics&quot; is a surface level argument, and a dumb one at that. It does mean there's accounting to be done, and certainly a rivalry to explore, but to pin them to the center of the mass of mythos would be...well, dumb and superficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-08-2019, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T12:18:15-07:00","id":1310786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310776#post1310776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) It's not written now. It was written over a decade ago with several books of built up mythology, structure, modes of operation, and more, and with that, the focus has been clarified and developed, and to arbitrarily go &quot;Well NOW we know about this game, so, you know, shove it in there&quot; feels pretty damn disingenuous compared to the clear theme it has.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 2E book is an opportunity to rewrite things to include things that where not in 1E, or otherwise make a major change in groups that could use it. AA is already getting what sounds like a major rewrite, and it isn't like all the other splats had a one-to-one conversion to the new edition. If it was just randomly thrown in on Mortal Remains &quot;Oh and AKD loves hunting Mummies and always had, we just never mentioned it until now&quot; it'd be weird. For the new book, it is something that could be fit in naturally. It'd be fair to compare it to the Lucifuge, who now have a new cosmology to work with and who will likely face some organic changes with the setting while keeping their core intact.<br /> <br /> If I where to complain about a group's focus that really didn't fit the theme, I'd say Mal Mal's ignoring Demons is super weird, given that the Catholic Church is a church and does exorcisms and the like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310776#post1310776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) You make it sound like that's not part of the design process. In this case, they started with the idiom of relics, which at the time covered werewolves, mages, and changelings. So they worked backwards to develop a story that was cool and evocative out of there, arrived at the destruction of a paradisical world, built into those themes(Because it is a major part of the text in Hunter 1E's Core, even if it's not the first part), cut out changelings because it didn't fit, and built their story from there. That's just how game design works. If you applied the same principle today, anyone looking for Cool, Evocative, and Weird is probably going to latch onto the same common root, and <i>maybe</i> create a hierarchy of enemies that allowed for emphasis on the Arisen, but would probably still give precedence to mages and werewolves</div> </div> </div> </div>I cheated by saying &quot;big books&quot;. Changling is a limited release book, and core hunter tended to work around the big three. You have core conspiracies that focus on vampires, mages, and werewolves, but you wouldn't have one focusing on promethians or changlings as they're limited release books and therefore hunting them would be more niche.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310776#post1310776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c) Just because something sounds <i>obvious</i> doesn't mean it always work. You have to take a long hard look at the tangle of things and see how it spins out to find the really strong thread, and then ruthlessly shave things out in the holy name of word count, and keep your focus on that core. Paradise Lost is a stronger thread than Oh Hey Relics, and can in fact better support Relics than Relics could support, say, Paradise Lost. With that said, some things get lost as a result of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly a writer, I could certainly imagine a writer would have writing problems that prevent things from coming around the obvious way. Oh Hey Relics is plenty a strong theme, they wrote a whole support book around that! I honestly don't think AKD would lose a lot of support if they dropped the Paradise Lost aspect and focused on the cool toys. When was the last time someone said &quot;Sure, that skull that can sink cities is cool and all, but my real love for AKD comes from the fact they're salty they lost Atlantis!&quot;<br /> <br /> If you take away the Paradise Lost aspect, then they are a group of humans who collects artifacts across the world to fight monsters. Indian Jones VS vampires. Still cool! Take way the Oh Hey Relics aspect and you have a bunch of dudes cutting up Werewolves because of jealousy and a vague sense of revenge. Meh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310776#post1310776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">d) In order to be horrifying, weird, tantalizing, and otherwise intriguing, what horror and comedy share is the twist of expectations. The sheer fact people complain about it without thinking about it but how it works with a little examination basically means the way AKD is now is a damn good fit for the dark mystery and horror angles of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We are the group known as the Wolfslayers. We kill vampires&quot; Ah yes, this twist makes the Wolfslayers perfect for dark mystery and horror.<br /> <br /> I can see where you're coming from, but am firm in the belief &quot;We gather powerful artifacts across the globe to keep the world safe and get us closer to paradise. Also we basically ignore a group that has powerful artifacts that would go perfectly in our vault and suit our goals, don't ask why, let's go kill some wolves instead&quot; is firmly in the &quot;comedy&quot; category. Sometimes things making sense makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310776#post1310776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;But They Both Care About Relics&quot; is a surface level argument and a dumb one at that. It does mean there's accounting to be done, and certainly a rivalry to explore, but to pin them to the center of the mass of mythos would be...well, dumb and superficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relationship being superficial would imply that relics are superficial in both, which really isn't the case. AKD are normal humans who want a taste of power. All their hatred of Mages and Werewolves is based around not having that power while others do. They take and steal power where they can find it, which happens to be artifacts. Mummies have a lot of power just lying around, why wouldn't they steal it to make themselves stronger? It is the logical outcome of their ideology.<br /> <br /> You keep calling it a &quot;means to an end&quot; like it isn't relevant, but &quot;what means are you willing to use?&quot; is a central theme to hunter as a whole. Like I said above, AKD really doesn't work without the relic aspect. You could switch it for another aspect and it'd still work. Switch their gimmick with Cheiron and they're still taking power from monsters in a different way, but they could still function as a group, but now they would switch their target since they wouldn't gain anything from fighting Mages. What they really want is power. Which they would get a lot of from stealing from mummies, so why not do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T14:02:04-07:00","id":1310807,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the &quot;AKD and relics&quot;, I just want to note that in Compacts and Conspiracies the Sword are presented as a faction which actually <i>had enough with relics</i>. C&amp;C (which is one of the best Hunter books, IMO, but I also like Witchfinders so take my word with a grain of salt) goes deep into the Paradise Lost theme and shows that for the AKD, relics are a reminder of what they claim was lost for them. It is their inheritance, sure- but it is also a reminder for their, and the world's, fallen state, and who is at fault for this.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that mummies can't get into this (relics as the inheritance of humanity may overlap with the way the Arisen treat the same relics as inheritance of Irem), but just like the MM hunts vampires first and the Lucifuge have a special hate toward demons, the AKD have their own enemies- and mummies never broke the world. Perhaps their creators changed the stars and forced kingship into the world together with messing up with time and memory, but they have never caused the world to fall from grace. Irem was far from a perfect utopia (more of Atlantis's negative, saying the truth), and the legacy it left behind is cursed for all eternity.<br /> <br /> I mean, Mortal Remains sums up pretty well the interaction between the AKD and mummies. Competition, game of cat and mouse, intelligence gathering and espionage. Making the AKD into specifically mummy hunters beyond what is already established instead of their shapeshifter focus earns little, IMO and cost a lot by diluting their themes into &quot;just relic hunters&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-08-2019, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T14:25:28-07:00","id":1310812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310807#post1310807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the &quot;AKD and relics&quot;, I just want to note that in Compacts and Conspiracies the Sword are presented as a faction which actually <i>had enough with relics</i>. C&amp;C (which is one of the best Hunter books, IMO, but I also like Witchfinders so take my word with a grain of salt) goes deep into the Paradise Lost theme and shows that for the AKD, relics are a reminder of what they claim was lost for them. It is their inheritance, sure- but it is also a reminder for their, and the world's, fallen state, and who is at fault for this.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that mummies can't get into this (relics as the inheritance of humanity may overlap with the way the Arisen treat the same relics as inheritance of Irem), but just like the MM hunts vampires first and the Lucifuge have a special hate toward demons, the AKD have their own enemies- and mummies never broke the world. Perhaps their creators changed the stars and forced kingship into the world together with messing up with time and memory, but they have never caused the world to fall from grace. Irem was far from a perfect utopia (more of Atlantis's negative, saying the truth), and the legacy it left behind is cursed for all eternity.<br /> <br /> I mean, Mortal Remains sums up pretty well the interaction between the AKD and mummies. Competition, game of cat and mouse, intelligence gathering and espionage. Making the AKD into specifically mummy hunters beyond what is already established instead of their shapeshifter focus earns little, IMO and cost a lot by diluting their themes into &quot;just relic hunters&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't really that they where sick of relics, it is that they want more than relics. Its basically just a paragraph about how they want &quot;real magic back&quot;, which seems like a pretty unobtainable goal. The same book also offered three backstories, two of which say they never had paradise in the first place and that the &quot;Paradise Fallen&quot; theme is just a lie &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> AKD doesn't really have any advanced interaction with any of their favored enemies. Just &quot;We vowed to kill them so we do. Some people occasionally don't do that when they don't want to&quot;, you really don't lose a lot by switching that to the cat-and-mouse espionage etc of the mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T15:34:59-07:00","id":1310828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310812#post1310812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't really that they where sick of relics, it is that they want more than relics. Its basically just a paragraph about how they want &quot;real magic back&quot;, which seems like a pretty unobtainable goal. The same book also offered three backstories, two of which say they never had paradise in the first place and that the &quot;Paradise Fallen&quot; theme is just a lie &gt;_&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div> It doesn't matter if the story is lie- as long as the conspiracy believes it to be true. The first one is the &quot;claimed&quot; story, and the other two are represented as its dark alternatives.<br /> <br /> Again, it is a matter of opinions- the AKD are &quot;indiana jones&quot; type hunters with and without mummies, and they will clash into the Arisen no matter what (again, Mortal Remains doesn't treat clashes with mummy cults as optional, but as something which will and does happen, whether the AKD want it or not). The thing is that if you remove shifters (and perhaps mages), as well as the whole backstory around which the AKD are built upon, you must then answer <i>why oh why would anyone want to hunt for relics- not to mention horde those terrible things all in one place</i>. I mean, not only that those things are <i>dangerous</i>- especially if you tie them to Mummy and then just touching them would curse you for all eternity- your enemies are <i>so far stronger than you.</i> I mean, sure, relics are useful- but without a really good reason why the hell will you put yourself in an everyday struggle against monsters which can rain fire from the sky, summon horrors from the abyss and turn to dust with a word, and that is if they feel creative and won't just tear you limb by limb. Not to mention that <i>they can not die</i>. Sure, curiosity can be a motive- for a compact. Conspiracies need something more than that- some unifying myth to hold them together against all chances, be it true or not.<br /> <br /> You want to rework the AKD into relic hunters which fight mummy cults? They already do it- it is just not their top priority (it's like, their second, considering that witches and shifters are on the same level). But even if you were to remove werewolves from their enemy list, mummies would still <i>remain at second place after mages</i>, as mummies never broke the world. If you want to remove all of the AKD's mythology and themes and make them focused only around relics, you need to give them a new reason to hunt after relics, which would mean a new ideology and new mythology. They will no longer be the &quot;Antediluvians&quot;, they will not have their oath of vengeance and will have an whole different backstory. In short, they will no longer be the Aegis Kai Doru in anything but the name- but an whole different conspiracy.<br /> <br /> In short, you can't just remove shifters and put mummies instead. It requires thought, a careful development if maintaining the true identity of the organization during the process. At the same level I could just remove vampire focus from the MM, throw away the Faceless Angels from the KoSG and turn Cheiron into decent human beings. I'm not saying it is not possible- but you need to be careful doing such things. Like, <i>careful</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T16:24:33-07:00","id":1310835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310828#post1310828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter if the story is lie- as long as the conspiracy believes it to be true. The first one is the &quot;claimed&quot; story, and the other two are represented as its dark alternatives.<br /> <br /> Again, it is a matter of opinions- the AKD are &quot;indiana jones&quot; type hunters with and without mummies, and they will clash into the Arisen no matter what (again, Mortal Remains doesn't treat clashes with mummy cults as optional, but as something which will and does happen, whether the AKD want it or not). The thing is that if you remove shifters (and perhaps mages), as well as the whole backstory around which the AKD are built upon, you must then answer <i>why oh why would anyone want to hunt for relics- not to mention horde those terrible things all in one place</i>. I mean, not only that those things are <i>dangerous</i>- especially if you tie them to Mummy and then just touching them would curse you for all eternity- your enemies are <i>so far stronger than you.</i> I mean, sure, relics are useful- but without a really good reason why the hell will you put yourself in an everyday struggle against monsters which can rain fire from the sky, summon horrors from the abyss and turn to dust with a word, and that is if they feel creative and won't just tear you limb by limb. Not to mention that <i>they can not die</i>. Sure, curiosity can be a motive- for a compact. Conspiracies need something more than that- some unifying myth to hold them together against all chances, be it true or not.<br /> <br /> You want to rework the AKD into relic hunters which fight mummy cults? They already do it- it is just not their top priority (it's like, their second, considering that witches and shifters are on the same level). But even if you were to remove werewolves from their enemy list, mummies would still <i>remain at second place after mages</i>, as mummies never broke the world. If you want to remove all of the AKD's mythology and themes and make them focused only around relics, you need to give them a new reason to hunt after relics, which would mean a new ideology and new mythology. They will no longer be the &quot;Antediluvians&quot;, they will not have their oath of vengeance and will have an whole different backstory. In short, they will no longer be the Aegis Kai Doru in anything but the name- but an whole different conspiracy.<br /> <br /> In short, you can't just remove shifters and put mummies instead. It requires thought, a careful development if maintaining the true identity of the organization during the process. At the same level I could just remove vampire focus from the MM, throw away the Faceless Angels from the KoSG and turn Cheiron into decent human beings. I'm not saying it is not possible- but you need to be careful doing such things. Like, <i>careful</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that I want them to be, just that it would be understandable if they got reworked. I ain't a writer, am not in any position to give advice, and can do whatever I want at my table anyway :P<br /> <br /> It just doesn't have much impact if &quot;You are actually just a puppet of the Acsending Ones/Pure/Secret Tier 4 Conspiracy&quot; is true. If your entire theme is paradise lost and you never had a paradise and never lost it, then the theme feels hollow. If your theme is &quot;Cool artifacts woosh woosh!&quot;, then it still works just fine, since you still have cool artifacts and get to use them. If they really just want the power given to them by the artifacts, then it doesn't matter if they are secretly working for mages because they already have what they want.<br /> <br /> For power? The same book has people eating mummies, and an anti-cult compact that (slightly-more-indirectly) fights mummies out of a sense of moral duty. There are plenty of other groups with plenty of other motivations that have them fight things much stronger than them. That is the whole point to being a hunter &gt;_&gt;. &quot;If you steal this amulet you will win any fight you find yourself in&quot; is a much more immediate motivator then &quot;Maybe one day you can reclaim your ancestor's glory!&quot;. Cheiron will face them for cash money. Its not like they're in a much better position picking on Awakened mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T22:19:56-07:00","id":1310923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310738#post1310738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not necessarily true. There's the optional 'The Ancient Vow Made Manifest' section from C&amp;C. Keeping in mind that the rules on Sleepwalkers are deliberately vague, I'd say that could satisfy the requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not read C&amp;C and am somewhat loath to buy it considering 2e is somewhere on the horizon. Is it worth purchasing, anyway, and/or can you summarize &quot;The Ancient Vow Made Manifest&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T23:04:10-07:00","id":1310930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310923#post1310923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have not read C&amp;C and am somewhat loath to buy it considering 2e is somewhere on the horizon. Is it worth purchasing, anyway, and/or can you summarize &quot;The Ancient Vow Made Manifest&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna take a second to say Yes, it is absolutely worth buying. It's actually my favorite supplement in the Hunter Line so far(Though Mortal Remains and Slasher <i>are</i> close).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T01:42:22-07:00","id":1310944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310923#post1310923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not read C&amp;C and am somewhat loath to buy it considering 2e is somewhere on the horizon. Is it worth purchasing, anyway, and/or can you summarize &quot;The Ancient Vow Made Manifest&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is substantially cheaper than most books (and only like 90 pages). It has some kinda dodgy stuff like the infamous vampires running Valkyrie, and much of it is labelled as 'optional', but at the same time I think I've read it multiple times so it's doing something right.<br /> <br /> That being said, TAVMM basically gives options for what would happen if the AKD oath had real metaphysical weight, including the Oath being the thing that allows AKD members to actually use relics, but also giving them buffs to fighting mages/werewolves. It is optional, but personally, I don't think the AKD make all that much sense without it because it directly ties their crusade against mages/werewolves to their ability to use relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T02:23:44-07:00","id":1310947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1310923#post1310923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have not read C&amp;C and am somewhat loath to buy it considering 2e is somewhere on the horizon. Is it worth purchasing, anyway, and/or can you summarize &quot;The Ancient Vow Made Manifest&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>C&amp;C is really awesome- it expands each of the core groups, giving some new plot hooks and optional mechanics to each of those. The AKD's expansion is really good, but it also has fun things about the Lucifuge and the others, and I personally really like the Ashwood Abbey's presentation as a pyramid scheme. The only reason I;m wary of telling you &quot;go get it RIGHT NOW&quot; is because we don't know how different the core groups will be in the new edition than how they are right now. I assume there will be some changes, but I hope there will be nothing too drastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T12:06:03-07:00","id":1311028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1309324#post1309324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with transhumanist leanings, I do <i>not</i> like the idea of a transhumanist Lucifuge. Before, they were about struggling to overcome what they were born into, and standing up for humankind; this seems to shift them towards &quot;I am better because I was born better&quot; powerfantasy. The ideal of transhumanism is lifting up oneself and others to overcome the frailties of what evolution gave us; being granted innately superior powers from birth, by circumstances outside your control, is the inverse of that. It is the aristocracy to transhumanism's meritocracy. What's more, the Lucifuges' humility, bordering on self-hatred, is what kept them from becoming superhero cliches. Hunter is about the worth of human life, and defending that candle against those that would snuff it out. Making a group about &quot;being born better than humans, and getting more better&quot; spits on that.</div> </div> </div> </div> You assume the Lucifuge are still Lucifuge by birth, instead of choice. From the Contagion Chronicles for example, it seems more based in a philosophy then bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 05-09-2019, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T13:14:29-07:00","id":1311043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311028#post1311028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You assume the Lucifuge are still Lucifuge by birth, instead of choice. From the Contagion Chronicles for example, it seems more based in a philosophy then bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean &quot;choosing to be Lucifuge&quot; as &quot;choosing the Vigil&quot;, or &quot;being a Lucifuge&quot; by &quot;having hellish powers&quot;? Because if it is the former, that's the situation more or less right now (even though the Lady leaves little choice between &quot;join&quot; and &quot;die&quot;). If the later, well.. being the literal son of a devil is such a core part of the Lucifuge's identity that it is hard for me to imagine it changed into just something that you join, considering the backlash it would probably create with the fans- not to mention the vast inconsistency it would do with the already 2e published material and that it would invalid so much of the former setting. Not to mention that from the playtests which featured the Lucifuge nothing seems to suggest a change in that direction.<br /> <br /> I mean, other than Geist, most of the 2e revisions didn't changed the very nature of the splats to that level, and as Hunter 2e is written by people who probably love the line, I doubt it will happen here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:03:57-07:00","id":1311068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311043#post1311043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean &quot;choosing to be Lucifuge&quot; as &quot;choosing the Vigil&quot;, or &quot;being a Lucifuge&quot; by &quot;having hellish powers&quot;? Because if it is the former, that's the situation more or less right now (even though the Lady leaves little choice between &quot;join&quot; and &quot;die&quot;). If the later, well.. being the literal son of a devil is such a core part of the Lucifuge's identity that it is hard for me to imagine it changed into just something that you join, considering the backlash it would probably create with the fans- not to mention the vast inconsistency it would do with the already 2e published material and that it would invalid so much of the former setting. Not to mention that from the playtests which featured the Lucifuge nothing seems to suggest a change in that direction.<br /> <br /> I mean, other than Geist, most of the 2e revisions didn't changed the very nature of the splats to that level, and as Hunter 2e is written by people who probably love the line, I doubt it will happen here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember what he was talking about from the playtest. Bringing it up, the &quot;Cassidy Tate&quot; character was used as an example of a character with zero dots in status but dots in the Endowment since the powers are something you are born with, as an example of a conspiracy where you can have more endowments then you do dots in status. The character herself was still a member without the status dot, so they are probably definitely keeping both the &quot;You're born with it&quot; and &quot;Join or Die&quot;. There has been non-Lucifuge demonspawn who can use some of their powers, and they have been stated since Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:53:17-07:00","id":1311084,"title":"","content":"Actually, they have been stated even before Inferno (unless you mean mechanically, and even then Inferno doesn't really give a solid system other than general guidelines, and you could always use Castigations to model them). Non Lucifuge 7th Generations have been stated since the core, right at the Enemy section, together with a conspiracy theory about the subject. Inferno just developed the idea into the L'Enfant Diabolique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:11:51-07:00","id":1311087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311084#post1311084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they have been stated even before Inferno (unless you mean mechanically, and even then Inferno doesn't really give a solid system other than general guidelines, and you could always use Castigations to model them). Non Lucifuge 7th Generations have been stated since the core, right at the Enemy section, together with a conspiracy theory about the subject. Inferno just developed the idea into the L'Enfant Diabolique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that as &quot;stat-ed&quot;, as much as anything else gets stat-ed in this series. Point is it was always a combination between having the powers and joining the group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:54:06-07:00","id":1311097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311087#post1311087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant that as &quot;stat-ed&quot;, as much as anything else gets stat-ed in this series. Point is it was always a combination between having the powers and joining the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word you're looking for is &quot;statted&quot; with two &quot;t&quot;s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T17:51:05-07:00","id":1311103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311097#post1311097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The word you're looking for is &quot;statted&quot; with two &quot;t&quot;s.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83e\udd26<br /> <br /> Go easy on me. The forum's spellcheck tells me it isn't a real word!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T18:11:25-07:00","id":1311107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311103#post1311103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \ud83e\udd26<br /> <br /> Go easy on me. The forum's spellcheck tells me it isn't a real word!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the way you're using the word &quot;stat&quot; (i.e. as a verb) is a slang term, so the past participle of the slang term is also a slang term, and therefore isn't in all dictionaries (especially one as lackluster as this forum's).<br /> <br /> Isn't English fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T14:40:12-07:00","id":1311287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1305603-a-possible-change-to-the-lucifuge?p=1311028#post1311028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You assume the Lucifuge are still Lucifuge by birth, instead of choice. From the Contagion Chronicles for example, it seems more based in a philosophy then bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referring to membership in the group, but rather the source of their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T15:38:22-07:00","id":1311297,"title":"","content":"I've always thought castigation was a power that only born lucifuge (demon spawn whatever we call them) could use once taught. At the very least it would make sense that for them to have an easier time using castigations than people not born with demonic blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T03:55:40-07:00","id":1312738,"title":"","content":"Since 1e I've been of the opinion that The Lucifuge needed to be something akin to the merit based templates from Hurt Locker, honestly as someone who's only read the core hunter book I felt there was too much content and wasn't enough to space (maybe time) to do justification to them all AKD is I believe one of the conspiracies that I felt needed a bit more work but I'm not sure what I wanted at the time. 2nd ed seems to be improving on first so I'm hopeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}